1
00:01:31,740 --> 00:01:33,975
So let's take a look at the same fate?

2
00:01:35,020 --> 00:01:38,040
Let's take a look at our wishes.

3
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:41,240
We are one of them.

4
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:05,010
What's that?

5
00:02:05,093 --> 00:02:09,417
There's a gigantic storm called Aqua
Laguna that's on its way here right now?

6
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:10,330
That's right!

7
00:02:10,413 --> 00:02:11,317
By midnight tonight,

8
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:14,837
this entire beach will be completely
underwater as well as half of the town!

9
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:15,750
Crazy, huh?

10
00:02:15,833 --> 00:02:16,663
That's terrible!

11
00:02:16,746 --> 00:02:18,157
We should get out of here right away!

12
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,070
Yes, sir!

13
00:02:19,153 --> 00:02:20,897
If we were smart, that's
exactly what we would do!

14
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:23,560
Let's evacuate to higher
ground! Good idea!

15
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:24,560
Let's do that!

16
00:02:25,280 --> 00:02:31,510
Evacuate!

17
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,230
That's weird.

18
00:02:49,313 --> 00:02:51,886
I could have sworn they
hurt someone out here!

19
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:54,537
Be sure to evacuate.

20
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:55,900
Evacuate, stop!

21
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:59,720
They were saying something about a storm?

22
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:04,320
Well, actually, the wind is
awfully strong, isn't it?

23
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:10,320
I'm telling you people, we
didn't do anything wrong!

24
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:11,817
You're making a mistake!

25
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:14,117
And why should we trust anything you say?

26
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:17,318
You scumbags are pirates
and probably assassins, too!

27
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:20,060
This doesn't even make any sense!

28
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:22,697
There's no reason why
Robin would attack him!

29
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:23,610
Yeah!

30
00:03:23,693 --> 00:03:27,912
Not only that, we'd never even heard
of Iceberg until we met him yesterday!

31
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:31,100
You brats just keep
saying that all you want.

32
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,510
It's over.

33
00:03:33,100 --> 00:03:35,520
Fact is, you picked on the wrong guy.

34
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:39,566
The moral of the story is, if
you make an enemy out of Iceberg,

35
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:42,957
then you make an enemy out of
the entire Galilag Company.

36
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:44,797
And that's not the half of it.

37
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:48,292
You also made an enemy out of
everyone in this whole city.

38
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:49,262
You understand?

39
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,597
Listen, I don't want to fight any of you.

40
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:53,974
We can still talk about all this, okay?

41
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:56,180
I don't give a damn what you want.

42
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:59,826
That's what you get for
messing with Kali-Lot!

43
00:04:21,900 --> 00:04:23,606
What's the matter, Straw Hat?

44
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:26,191
You're not even gonna go out with a fight?

45
00:04:26,460 --> 00:04:27,860
I just told you!

46
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:31,215
We're not enemies and I don't
want to fight any of you!

47
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:37,267
Since pistols don't work on you,
we'll have to go with plan B.

48
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:40,920
Damn it all!

49
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:43,551
I guess these guys are going all out, huh?

50
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:54,380
No, he got away.

51
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:59,300
Wow, they almost had me.

52
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:29,240
Oh, I can't dodge anymore!

53
00:05:34,960 --> 00:05:36,597
Yeah, that's right!

54
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:38,000
All right, nice shot!

55
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:48,390
Yeah!

56
00:05:50,360 --> 00:05:54,337
And that's why Galley-La
are pride and joy! Woo!

57
00:05:54,420 --> 00:05:56,700
It feels good to see them lose.

58
00:05:57,540 --> 00:06:01,240
I hope they blow that
sorry sucker sky high!

59
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:10,840
Nah, I shouldn't say that after
all Straw Hats, our enemy, too,

60
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:13,864
and I haven't beaten him
nearly enough, not yet.

61
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:17,540
And to be fair, I was here first.

62
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,877
Wasn't I I?

63
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:25,840
I enjoyed your little show, but this is
my stage and the only star here is Franky.

64
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:28,980
So get out of my!

65
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:35,737
Hold your horses we'll
be done with them in a

66
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:38,938
second then you can fight
us to your heart's content.

67
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:44,237
Listen you I called dibs on straw
hat before all of you even got here?

68
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,500
No, screw it.

69
00:06:46,700 --> 00:06:49,020
You don't even care what I say, do you?

70
00:06:49,400 --> 00:06:50,600
Paulie, watch out!

71
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:52,300
Get out of there!

72
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:54,637
Frankie's going nuts again!

73
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:55,550
Run away!

74
00:06:56,260 --> 00:06:57,090
Huh?

75
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,420
Connector set.

76
00:07:07,180 --> 00:07:10,360
He brought down a crane with
that attack. It's lethal!

77
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:11,800
That was him?

78
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:14,217
Looks like a cannon hit it.

79
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:15,440
He's about to fire!

80
00:07:16,460 --> 00:07:17,700
Get him broke!

81
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:19,409
Your cannon's ready to go!

82
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:20,350
Hey!

83
00:07:20,433 --> 00:07:23,141
Don't expect me to shoot
a cannonball or anything.

84
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:26,080
The shells I fire are
made of nothing but air.

85
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:29,440
Still, these babies
break the speed of sound.

86
00:07:30,380 --> 00:07:31,360
Air, huh?

87
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:35,400
Run for your lives!

88
00:07:41,920 --> 00:07:43,900
What the hell?

89
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:39,300
Man, he was a kitten.

90
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:42,127
That thing hits like a
hurricane to the face.

91
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:45,080
Another brain is coming down!

92
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,320
Get out of here!

93
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:48,560
It's gonna fall on us!

94
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:52,390
Hurry up!

95
00:08:52,473 --> 00:08:53,480
Here it comes!

96
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:59,360
Yeah, let it fall!

97
00:09:00,380 --> 00:09:01,920
Hell, I don't care.

98
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:04,840
Let's bring the whole damn shipyard down!

99
00:09:21,140 --> 00:09:22,957
He really is a cyborg.

100
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,137
I thought he was kidding.

101
00:09:24,220 --> 00:09:25,937
But that air shot was no joke.

102
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:28,737
I've never even seen technology like that.

103
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:30,597
But hey.

104
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:34,197
No more angry mom. At least.

105
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:35,400
Nami, run!

106
00:09:35,780 --> 00:09:38,600
Luffy, you didn't get
hit back there, did you?

107
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:43,794
It's gonna take a lot more than that
if those guys want to get rid of me.

108
00:09:44,600 --> 00:09:45,600
Okay, come on.

109
00:09:45,760 --> 00:09:46,878
We gotta get going.

110
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:49,997
I'm not sure how, but we
gotta talk to Ice Pops.

111
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:51,080
What? Now?

112
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:54,060
When the whole town is
out searching for us?

113
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:55,937
Hey, look!

114
00:09:56,020 --> 00:09:57,491
Straw Hat's getting away!

115
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:58,750
Uh-oh.

116
00:09:58,833 --> 00:10:00,585
They're trying to surround us.

117
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:02,370
Nami!

118
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:07,740
Hey, hold on tight, okay?

119
00:10:08,060 --> 00:10:09,180
No, not okay!

120
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:10,640
Stop them!

121
00:10:17,060 --> 00:10:18,180
They're too fast!

122
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,180
Follow them!

123
00:10:23,760 --> 00:10:24,590
Bro?

124
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:29,896
They're getting away, don't
you want to go after them?

125
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:34,540
Ah, that last coup de vin
did ate up all my fuel.

126
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:35,920
You see this?

127
00:10:36,120 --> 00:10:37,340
My pompadour's limp.

128
00:10:37,940 --> 00:10:38,770
No kidding.

129
00:10:38,980 --> 00:10:41,509
It looks like a willow
swaying in the wind.

130
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:45,360
What a mess, stupid Galley-La.

131
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:49,681
But I'll take care of that straw
hat as soon as I'm done refueling.

132
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,720
That kid ain't half bad, you know?

133
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:55,979
He certainly earned his big bounty.

134
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:03,957
Jeez Louise.

135
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:06,360
Even for Franky, this is too much.

136
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:08,560
Today just isn't our day.

137
00:11:09,320 --> 00:11:12,438
Franky or no Franky, we
can't let Straw Hat escape.

138
00:11:13,060 --> 00:11:15,100
Aqua Laguna is gonna hit tonight.

139
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:18,400
There are only two sea
train departures left today.

140
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:21,420
Since the Straw Hats
can't leave on their ship,

141
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:24,777
the Sea Train's the only ticket
they've got to get off the island.

142
00:11:24,860 --> 00:11:26,197
This is our chance.

143
00:11:26,280 --> 00:11:30,420
Have every member of Galley-La
spread out and hunt them down.

144
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:33,080
We'll settle this before sunset.

145
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:47,500
Granny, look!

146
00:11:47,780 --> 00:11:48,880
It's Water 7!

147
00:11:51,500 --> 00:11:54,620
Don't get too excited and
fall in the ocean now.

148
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:10,500
If that isn't Galley-La
HQ, I don't know what is.

149
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:13,920
No surprise, since it's right
next to Dock 1. And look!

150
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:17,627
The place is totally
swarming with reporters.

151
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:21,041
Those tough-looking guys
are probably shipwrights.

152
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,767
I'm willing to bet that's
where Iceberg's at.

153
00:12:28,020 --> 00:12:29,457
You sure about this?

154
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,217
Of course, I am.

155
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:33,577
The only way for me to
find out what's going on

156
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:36,197
between Ice Pops and Robin
is to ask him myself.

157
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:37,977
I can't stop you,

158
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:40,017
but you should keep in
mind that everyone on

159
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:42,157
the island is trying to
hunt us down right now.

160
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:44,577
So listen before you do anything rash.

161
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:46,697
Sneak around and figure
out where Icebergs'

162
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:48,457
room is so you know where you need to go.

163
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:50,540
All right. I'm off.

164
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:57,240
What? No!

165
00:12:57,620 --> 00:12:58,855
They can't find them.

166
00:13:05,380 --> 00:13:06,360
Who's that?

167
00:13:06,720 --> 00:13:08,360
Wait, it can't be!

168
00:13:14,540 --> 00:13:16,140
Someone broke the window!

169
00:13:17,460 --> 00:13:19,060
We're under attack!

170
00:13:20,840 --> 00:13:22,540
Straw Hat Luffy broken!

171
00:13:22,820 --> 00:13:24,620
He must be after Iceberg!

172
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:27,797
He's doing this in the middle of the day?

173
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:30,174
He's got some guts coming after us now.

174
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:31,280
Where is he?

175
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:34,307
He's taking the stairs
up to the third floor.

176
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:35,477
Where are the foremen?

177
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:37,297
They all spread out
looking for Straw Hats.

178
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:38,262
No one is here.

179
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:41,280
He's wearing a red vest.

180
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:42,558
You can't miss him.

181
00:13:43,040 --> 00:13:45,160
Don't let him get to Iceberg.

182
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:48,360
I found us.

183
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:53,040
Hey, over here.

184
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:55,450
Where is he?

185
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:56,460
Where is he?

186
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:08,200
Don't shoot a pistol,
you idiot! We're inside!

187
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:09,817
You're gonna disturb Mr.

188
00:14:09,900 --> 00:14:10,730
Iceberg!

189
00:14:12,720 --> 00:14:14,400
I know you need to rest.

190
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:16,480
I apologize for the commotion.

191
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:18,260
Well, what's going on?

192
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:23,727
Apparently, Straw Hat Luffy has
broken in and is running amok.

193
00:14:25,340 --> 00:14:28,480
In that case, I have a plan.

194
00:14:32,020 --> 00:14:32,960
Found him!

195
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:38,360
Whoa, there's a lot of shipwrites!

196
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:40,557
He's going to building two!

197
00:14:40,640 --> 00:14:41,470
Follow him!

198
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,040
Lupi, wait!

199
00:14:53,780 --> 00:14:54,610
It's you!

200
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:59,277
Khalifa, did you see a
pirate come this way?

201
00:14:59,360 --> 00:15:01,000
If I had, then you'd know.

202
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:04,000
And by the way, you're far too noisy. Mr.

203
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:06,197
Iceberg still needs his peace and quiet.

204
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,110
You're right.

205
00:15:07,193 --> 00:15:08,023
Sorry.

206
00:15:08,106 --> 00:15:10,197
Looks like the Straw Hat
hasn't made it this far yet.

207
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:12,037
Let's stay and watch around this hallway.

208
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:14,179
This is where he's headed for sure.

209
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:27,677
Well hello there, pirate boy.

210
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,277
Were you looking for me?

211
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:30,617
Sure was.

212
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:32,900
Thanks for saving me from those guys.

213
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:37,917
Considering the angry mob, I assume that
you didn't burst in here just to murder me.

214
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,617
All I want is to hear
your side of the story.

215
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:44,357
Last night I saw Nico Robin here.

216
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:45,381
Without a doubt.

217
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:50,597
And mind you, I have
nothing against any of you.

218
00:15:50,680 --> 00:15:52,677
I have no reason to lie.

219
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:55,377
Are you sure it wasn't
someone who looked like her?

220
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:57,057
Shut up and listen, boy.

221
00:15:57,140 --> 00:16:01,517
I didn't call you in here to
bicker about who did what.

222
00:16:01,600 --> 00:16:06,497
I have a favor to ask, and it would
be in your best interest to grant it.

223
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:09,777
No matter what it takes.

224
00:16:09,860 --> 00:16:12,100
I have to see Niko-Robin again.

225
00:16:14,020 --> 00:16:15,720
We're here! We're here!

226
00:16:15,900 --> 00:16:18,980
Come on, Granny! Hurry! Hurry! Calm down.

227
00:16:19,280 --> 00:16:20,660
Get a hold of yourself.

228
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:25,320
Water 7.

229
00:16:25,820 --> 00:16:30,860
It's been a while. Granny!
Hurry! Hurry! Okay! Okay!

230
00:16:31,900 --> 00:16:33,420
Attention all passengers!

231
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:36,617
Wearing a mask on the Sea Train
today is strictly prohibited.

232
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:39,017
Look, ma 'am, just cooperate
and show me your face.

233
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:40,740
This is my face. See?

234
00:16:43,440 --> 00:16:44,340
Hey, you.

235
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:47,160
Oh, uh, Miss Kokoro.

236
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,417
So nice to see you again.

237
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:50,265
What's going on here, trouble?

238
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:51,600
Yes, yes, ma 'am.

239
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:53,877
Everyone is on the lookout
for the Straw Hat Pirates,

240
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:57,195
the culprits in the attempted
assassination of Iceberg.

241
00:16:57,740 --> 00:16:58,916
Iceberg's assassins?

242
00:16:59,620 --> 00:17:01,700
What is it, Granny? Huh?

243
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:03,960
Hey, wait a minute.

244
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,917
I'll say it once again!

245
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:13,297
Let me see, Nico Robin?

246
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:16,317
Sorry, that's not possible.

247
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:19,500
We have no idea where she is.

248
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:27,310
Gunfire!

249
00:17:27,740 --> 00:17:29,340
It came from the bedroom!

250
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:35,600
Icebird! We heard it!

251
00:17:42,740 --> 00:17:44,160
Are you all right?

252
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,270
Yes.

253
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:49,417
I'd hoped to come closer to the truth.

254
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:51,794
But that foolish hope has been in vain.

255
00:17:52,720 --> 00:17:55,200
Arrest all of the Straw Hat Pirates.

256
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:56,890
Yes, sir!

257
00:18:01,140 --> 00:18:02,060
Hey, Luffy.

258
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:04,737
Were you able to speak with Iceberg?

259
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:05,650
What did he say?

260
00:18:05,733 --> 00:18:07,100
Is it true? Yeah.

261
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:10,340
He said it was Robin,
no doubt of it. No way.

262
00:18:10,740 --> 00:18:12,837
Why would she do something like that?

263
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,700
I refuse to believe it.

264
00:18:35,720 --> 00:18:38,360
